WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.744
What happens inside a neural network?

2
00:00:03.124 --> 00:00:04.306
Let's open one up.

3
00:00:05.256 --> 00:00:07.770
One neuron multiplies each input by a

4
00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.536
weight, adds a bias, and squashes the

5
00:00:10.536 --> 00:00:12.150
total with an activation.

6
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.374
The activation decides how strongly

7
00:00:15.374 --> 00:00:17.912
the neuron fires: the sigmoid, the

8
00:00:17.912 --> 00:00:19.718
tanh, or the simple ReLU.

9
00:00:20.668 --> 00:00:22.510
Join many neurons in layers

10
00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:24.082
and you have a network.

11
00:00:24.462 --> 00:00:26.820
Data flows forward, and the error

12
00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:28.836
flows back to fix the weights.

13
00:00:29.786 --> 00:00:31.898
Training repeats this many times.

14
00:00:32.278 --> 00:00:34.564
Watch the boundary bend around the

15
00:00:34.564 --> 00:00:36.634
inner circle as the loss falls.

16
00:00:37.584 --> 00:00:39.882
Each update is a step downhill on

17
00:00:39.882 --> 00:00:42.306
the error, like a ball rolling to

18
00:00:42.306 --> 00:00:43.878
the bottom of a valley.

19
00:00:44.828 --> 00:00:47.618
For pictures, convolution layers scan for

20
00:00:47.618 --> 00:00:50.192
edges and shapes, then pooling layers

21
00:00:50.192 --> 00:00:52.922
shrink the picture before the final guess.

22
00:00:53.872 --> 00:00:55.918
Language models use transformers:

23
00:00:56.098 --> 00:00:58.720
attention lets every word look at every

24
00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.414
other word, and the block repeats many

25
00:01:01.414 --> 00:01:01.804
times.

26
00:01:02.754 --> 00:01:04.944
In the end the model gives each

27
00:01:04.944 --> 00:01:07.362
picture a class and how sure it is.

28
00:01:07.742 --> 00:01:09.638
Always check the unsure ones.

29
00:01:10.588 --> 00:01:12.724
Neurons, layers, training and

30
00:01:12.724 --> 00:01:15.124
architecture: now you've seen inside.
